    "title": "How is artificial intelligence affecting Chicago workers? - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Patrick Smith ,\n8 hours ago Experts are split on what A.I. will ultimately mean for the workforce, and WBEZ listeners weigh in. Goldman Sachs predicts that machine-learning could replace 300 million jobs. But the Federal Reserve Bank of Chicago says it’s more likely artificial intelligence will lead to job changes, not necessarily job loss. What everyone agrees on is that Americans are very worried about how A.I. will affect the workforce. According to the Chicago Fed, “50 percent of Americans are more concerned than excited about the increased use of A.I..” Read full article",
